1
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:05,621
Two national parks in one day!

2
00:00:05,621 --> 00:00:08,914
More than 2,000 natural stone arches.

3
00:00:08,914 --> 00:00:12,831
A cliff 2,000 feet above the Colorado River.

4
00:00:12,831 --> 00:00:16,570
And a whole world of canyons at your feet!

5
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:23,795
This is Moab to Arches and Canyonlands: about 65 miles through Utah's red rock playground.

6
00:00:23,795 --> 00:00:27,420
Stick around till the end for the full trip planner!

7
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:29,571
Here's the plan!

8
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:36,930
We start in Moab, then Arches, Dead Horse Point, and we finish at Grand View Point in Canyonlands!

9
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:41,789
We're starting in Moab, base camp for two national parks!

10
00:00:41,789 --> 00:00:46,110
Rent a jeep, ride a mountain bike, or float the Colorado River.

11
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:53,410
North out of Moab, past the visitor center, and up the switchbacks into Arches!

12
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:56,641
Welcome to Arches National Park!

13
00:00:56,641 --> 00:00:59,278
More than 2,000 natural stone arches.

14
00:00:59,278 --> 00:01:04,980
Walk out to the Windows, and if you have time, hike to Delicate Arch for sunset!

15
00:01:05,930 --> 00:01:10,560
Back out of Arches, then up Highway 313 onto the mesa top!

16
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:13,161
This is Dead Horse Point!

17
00:01:13,161 --> 00:01:17,782
Two thousand feet straight down to a giant bend in the Colorado River.

18
00:01:17,782 --> 00:01:22,140
The famous ending of Thelma and Louise was filmed right near here!

19
00:01:23,090 --> 00:01:27,300
Into Canyonlands National Park, out along the Island in the Sky!

20
00:01:29,690 --> 00:01:34,341
We made it to Grand View Point, in Canyonlands National Park!

21
00:01:34,341 --> 00:01:41,204
Layer after layer of canyons drop away below you, carved by the Colorado and Green Rivers.

22
00:01:41,204 --> 00:01:43,720
On the way, don't miss Mesa Arch!

23
00:01:44,670 --> 00:01:46,407
And that's the drive!

24
00:01:46,407 --> 00:01:51,700
About 65 miles, two national parks, and a whole lot of red rock.

25
00:01:52,650 --> 00:01:56,028
Here's your trip planner, everything in one place.

26
00:01:56,028 --> 00:01:57,920
Pause and grab a screenshot!

27
00:02:01,150 --> 00:02:02,726
Thanks for riding along!

28
00:02:02,726 --> 00:02:10,740
Subscribe to Road Trip Atlas for more Utah road trips, and next time we're heading to Monument Valley and the Moki Dugway!
